        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "overview",
      "title": "Overview",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "The human voice is the oldest instrument — sung, spoken, and shouted across every culture. Classified as aerophone (lungs provide air; vocal folds vibrate)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "registers",
      "title": "Registers",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Chest voice (modal register), head voice, falsetto, whistle register. Passaggio — transition points between registers."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "voice-types",
      "title": "Voice types",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Soprano, mezzo, alto/contralto, tenor, baritone, bass — choral classification. Folk singing ignores Fach categories; find comfortable range."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "styles",
      "title": "Styles",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Opera bel canto. Gospel and blues growl. Sean-nós unaccompanied Irish song. Shape-note hymnody. Throat singing (Tuva, Mongolia)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "health",
      "title": "Health",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Hydration, warm-up, rest. Hoarseness lasting >2 weeks warrants medical attention."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
